>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_backend`

``` hol4
Refute.register_backend : backend -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds or replaces a Refute search backend.

``` hol4
type backend =
  {name : string,
   weight : int,
   configured : unit -> bool,
   requires : requirement,
   input : goal_form,
   certainty_ceiling : config -> instance list -> certainty,
   run : config -> instance list -> outcome}
```

A backend replaces any registered backend of the same `name`, and is
selected by `RegisteredBackend name`.  Backends run in increasing
`weight` order, ties broken by name, when the search is sequential;
`configured ()` says whether the backend is available.  `requires` is
`AnyGoal`, `ExecutableGoal`, or `ExecutableGoalUnless p`, which also
accepts a non-executable goal when `p cfg instances` holds.  `input`
is `MonoInstances` or `PolyOriginal`.

`certainty_ceiling` must bound from above the certainty `run` can
return: a search stops once a result reaches the best ceiling of the
selected backends, so an underestimate can hide a stronger result.
`fn _ => fn _ => Genuine` is always safe.

Exceptions and timeouts in `run` become `Unknown`.  `run` must not
start a nested Refute search; one that does gets `Unknown`.
Registrations last for the session.

